1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:01,680
[Previously]
Sometimes, the truth hurts.

2
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:05,240
Yi killed my dad.

3
00:00:06,714 --> 00:00:07,960
Yi has passed away.

4
00:00:09,715 --> 00:00:11,320
But if we refuse to accept it,

5
00:00:11,368 --> 00:00:13,169
we'll never be able to make things right.

6
00:00:13,422 --> 00:00:15,238
I guess there's really no way
to fix things anymore.

7
00:00:15,262 --> 00:00:17,640
Because the Kongpurim
and Monchaitrakul families

8
00:00:18,088 --> 00:00:19,489
will never be able to reconcile.

9
00:00:20,392 --> 00:00:21,832
Send someone to help Pakkard! Hurry!

10
00:00:21,875 --> 00:00:23,560
They've found Pakkard!

11
00:01:11,403 --> 00:01:12,404
Hey!

12
00:01:21,100 --> 00:01:25,100
"Juliet &amp; Juliet" (Episode 8)

13
00:01:27,654 --> 00:01:28,843
Let me go, you bastard!

14
00:01:29,531 --> 00:01:30,532
Go!

15
00:02:01,321 --> 00:02:02,322
You bitch!

16
00:02:11,184 --> 00:02:15,200
I gave you a scholarship
and paid for your education!

17
00:02:15,931 --> 00:02:18,560
And this is how you repay me, huh?

18
00:02:20,880 --> 00:02:22,081
Is this how you repay me?

19
00:02:23,899 --> 00:02:25,500
Don't act all nice, you old bastard!

20
00:02:26,616 --> 00:02:28,000
You expect me to thank you?

21
00:02:29,182 --> 00:02:31,440
What about your son Yi killing my father?

22
00:02:31,445 --> 00:02:33,046
Your father deserved to die!

23
00:02:34,460 --> 00:02:36,061
And so do you, bitch!

24
00:02:41,355 --> 00:02:42,675
If you're going to shoot Pakkard,

25
00:02:46,700 --> 00:02:48,000
you'll have to kill me first!

26
00:02:52,944 --> 00:02:54,650
Taking your revenge out on me

27
00:02:55,846 --> 00:02:57,760
would be much more satisfying.

28
00:03:03,248 --> 00:03:05,600
This bitch is even braver than her father!

29
00:03:06,822 --> 00:03:07,880
Blue!

30
00:03:10,368 --> 00:03:11,680
Don't worry.

31
00:03:12,369 --> 00:03:14,080
Since you've got the guts to come forward,

32
00:03:14,528 --> 00:03:15,960
I've got the guts to take you on!

33
00:03:16,900 --> 00:03:17,901
Big!

34
00:03:19,416 --> 00:03:20,760
Call Wiboon.

35
00:03:21,438 --> 00:03:23,400
Tell him I've got his daughter.

36
00:03:24,659 --> 00:03:26,560
After 17 years of hatred,

37
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:29,520
it's finally time to settle the score.

38
00:03:34,683 --> 00:03:35,760
But as for you, bitch,

39
00:03:41,451 --> 00:03:43,251
I don't have to wait
for that bastard Wiboon!

40
00:03:47,838 --> 00:03:48,839
Dad, don't!

41
00:03:55,900 --> 00:03:57,720
You're still trying to protect her, huh?

42
00:04:00,072 --> 00:04:01,073
No.

43
00:04:03,630 --> 00:04:04,880
But the person who killed Mom

44
00:04:06,462 --> 00:04:07,840
wasn't Pakkard's father.

45
00:04:10,670 --> 00:04:12,320
If it wasn't Wirat, then who was it?

46
00:04:13,576 --> 00:04:15,496
He was the only one
who had a grudge against me!

47
00:04:17,059 --> 00:04:19,060
If Mom really had run away with Wirat,

48
00:04:20,822 --> 00:04:22,760
the only person who stood to lose anything

49
00:04:25,963 --> 00:04:27,200
was Blue's father.

50
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,001
Wiboon?

51
00:04:50,201 --> 00:04:51,602
Blue! Blue!

52
00:05:17,024 --> 00:05:18,325
Hang in there, okay?

53
00:05:18,432 --> 00:05:19,433
You...

54
00:05:26,220 --> 00:05:27,880
Breathe. Just breathe. Come on.

55
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,900
- Blue!
- Blue!

56
00:05:33,382 --> 00:05:35,320
Blue! Blue!

57
00:05:35,691 --> 00:05:36,692
Blue!

58
00:05:36,912 --> 00:05:39,280
Stay with me, Blue.

59
00:05:39,325 --> 00:05:40,920
Stay with Mom.

60
00:05:41,558 --> 00:05:42,760
Blue!

61
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:48,360
Will my death

62
00:05:49,355 --> 00:05:51,200
finally put an end to all this?

63
00:05:55,628 --> 00:05:57,640
Let it end here, Dad.

64
00:06:12,560 --> 00:06:15,200
Blue! Blue! Blue!

65
00:06:15,278 --> 00:06:16,279
Blue!

66
00:06:18,760 --> 00:06:19,761
Blue!

67
00:06:21,902 --> 00:06:22,903
Po! You son of a bitch!

68
00:06:23,192 --> 00:06:24,193
Get down!

69
00:06:36,312 --> 00:06:37,760
Tokyo, run!

70
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:40,160
- Go! - Go!

71
00:06:55,470 --> 00:06:56,471
Stop!

72
00:06:57,566 --> 00:06:58,680
Drop your weapons!

73
00:07:00,808 --> 00:07:02,088
Put your hands behind your head!

74
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:04,321
Take them away!

75
00:07:55,611 --> 00:07:57,200
Hang in there, Pakkard.

76
00:07:58,230 --> 00:07:59,800
I'm trying to find a way to help you.

77
00:08:03,451 --> 00:08:04,960
Please don't, Aunt Ratri.

78
00:08:06,758 --> 00:08:08,500
Just let me stay here.

79
00:08:09,182 --> 00:08:10,360
Don't bail me out.

80
00:08:14,072 --> 00:08:15,352
When you choose to do something,

81
00:08:16,088 --> 00:08:19,360
you have to be willing
to face the consequences.

82
00:08:22,870 --> 00:08:23,871
Are you sure about this?

83
00:08:25,008 --> 00:08:27,600
Life in there won't be easy.

84
00:08:31,840 --> 00:08:35,041
I'd rather stay in here
than spend the rest of my life

85
00:08:35,334 --> 00:08:36,335
hiding out there.

86
00:08:39,147 --> 00:08:41,360
This is for the best.

87
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:47,281
It's how things should be.

88
00:09:06,979 --> 00:09:07,980
Okay.

89
00:09:15,419 --> 00:09:18,360
The police said they need to issue
an arrest warrant for Tokyo.

90
00:09:22,995 --> 00:09:24,600
There's nothing I can do, Dad.

91
00:09:32,236 --> 00:09:34,236
What the fuck are you
grunting about, you bastard?

92
00:09:42,168 --> 00:09:44,169
Don't think this is going to end so easily!

93
00:10:10,200 --> 00:10:11,801
[Monica Phakjira Monchaitrakul]

94
00:10:22,700 --> 00:10:24,838
Do you even feel any grief
over our daughter's death?

95
00:10:27,243 --> 00:10:28,560
What do you mean by that?

96
00:10:30,454 --> 00:10:31,455
Our daughter died

97
00:10:32,731 --> 00:10:35,360
because you were blinded
by your thirst for revenge!

98
00:10:37,729 --> 00:10:39,120
Are you taking their side now?

99
00:10:40,513 --> 00:10:41,520
Everything I've done

100
00:10:42,475 --> 00:10:44,275
was for the sake of our
Monchaitrakul family!

101
00:10:47,066 --> 00:10:48,280
For the sake of our family?

102
00:10:51,680 --> 00:10:52,681
Or for yourself?

103
00:12:00,843 --> 00:12:02,483
Have you heard anything from your sister?

104
00:12:02,872 --> 00:12:04,432
I still haven't been able to reach her.

105
00:12:04,918 --> 00:12:06,100
But don't worry, Dad.

106
00:12:07,344 --> 00:12:09,400
I'll send our men out to look for her.

107
00:12:11,340 --> 00:12:14,041
You're so fucking useless, you bastard!

108
00:12:15,115 --> 00:12:16,416
Oh, Dad!

109
00:12:21,723 --> 00:12:23,960
We don't even know if
your sister is dead or alive!

110
00:12:24,624 --> 00:12:27,144
And you, her useless excuse for a brother,
can still stay calm?

111
00:12:29,163 --> 00:12:32,320
I know the Monchaitrakuls
haven't found her either.

112
00:12:34,619 --> 00:12:37,040
She's still safe, Dad. Don't worry.

113
00:12:42,723 --> 00:12:44,480
The fact that no one knows where Tokyo is

114
00:12:45,859 --> 00:12:47,059
is actually a good thing, Dad.

115
00:12:48,659 --> 00:12:50,099
What the hell are you talking about?

116
00:12:50,976 --> 00:12:52,600
If the police catch her,

117
00:12:52,667 --> 00:12:53,800
she'll end up in prison.

118
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:58,200
But if she's unlucky enough to get caught
by those Monchaitrakul bastards first,

119
00:12:58,720 --> 00:13:02,160
- she could end up dead, Dad!
- That's why we need to find her!

120
00:13:05,312 --> 00:13:09,960
Are you going to let the
Kongpurim family lose another heir?

121
00:13:12,700 --> 00:13:15,760
Your brother Yi is already dead!

122
00:13:19,701 --> 00:13:20,702
What about me, Dad?

123
00:13:29,766 --> 00:13:32,000
I've already mapped out your future.

124
00:13:32,528 --> 00:13:34,250
You're supposed to be a police officer

125
00:13:34,560 --> 00:13:36,120
and support your siblings.

126
00:13:42,462 --> 00:13:43,880
But if Tokyo doesn't come back...

127
00:13:47,463 --> 00:13:49,464
That's not for you to
worry about right now!

128
00:13:49,912 --> 00:13:51,300
Your job right now

129
00:13:51,990 --> 00:13:53,491
is to find your sister!

130
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:59,001
Go!

131
00:14:47,907 --> 00:14:50,680
Will you two stop this madness already?

132
00:14:52,059 --> 00:14:53,992
If this keeps going on,

133
00:14:54,776 --> 00:14:56,520
I can't let you stay here any longer.

134
00:15:02,019 --> 00:15:03,760
But I didn't start it this time, sir.

135
00:15:06,384 --> 00:15:07,560
Maybe not this time.

136
00:15:08,571 --> 00:15:09,760
But what about before?

137
00:15:10,507 --> 00:15:12,600
Can you swear you never started anything?

138
00:15:17,750 --> 00:15:20,800
With the upcoming election,

139
00:15:21,350 --> 00:15:23,320
I'm not risking my
career because of you two.

140
00:15:25,283 --> 00:15:26,520
I've made my decision.

141
00:15:27,920 --> 00:15:28,960
From now on,

142
00:15:29,902 --> 00:15:31,503
I'm cutting both families out

143
00:15:31,550 --> 00:15:33,751
of the port concession business.

144
00:15:34,500 --> 00:15:35,108
But sir...

145
00:15:35,132 --> 00:15:36,980
I didn't call you here to ask for your opinions.

146
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:38,440
This is an order.

147
00:15:39,100 --> 00:15:40,443
That's not fair, sir.

148
00:15:40,752 --> 00:15:42,240
The Monchaitrakuls started it.

149
00:15:42,534 --> 00:15:44,000
The Kongpurims did nothing wrong.

150
00:15:44,366 --> 00:15:45,400
But all this time,

151
00:15:46,094 --> 00:15:48,440
the Monchaitrakul family
has been the one getting bullied.

152
00:15:51,998 --> 00:15:55,000
And now, the public is
throwing its support behind

153
00:15:55,168 --> 00:15:57,069
a progressive like me,

154
00:15:59,856 --> 00:16:01,760
not the old guard like before.

155
00:16:04,395 --> 00:16:05,640
Your approval ratings

156
00:16:06,416 --> 00:16:07,840
have been steadily rising

157
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:10,050
because of me, sir.

158
00:16:17,334 --> 00:16:19,300
You're not the only one

159
00:16:19,440 --> 00:16:21,140
who can be progressive, you know.

160
00:16:22,496 --> 00:16:27,640
Do you really think I can't find
one or two more people like you?

161
00:16:35,331 --> 00:16:36,371
So, what's it going to be?

162
00:16:37,123 --> 00:16:38,700
How about we both take a step back?

163
00:16:50,220 --> 00:16:53,080
I can have the arrest warrant
for your daughter withdrawn.

164
00:16:55,200 --> 00:16:57,401
But you'll have to leave this city

165
00:16:59,782 --> 00:17:01,450
and bid for concessions elsewhere.

166
00:17:02,859 --> 00:17:04,939
I'll put in a good word for
you with my connections.

167
00:17:06,397 --> 00:17:07,398
As for you,

168
00:17:08,483 --> 00:17:09,760
Monchaitrakul,

169
00:17:10,472 --> 00:17:12,360
it's time to stop obsessing over the past.

170
00:17:28,387 --> 00:17:32,200
In the end, the Monchaitrakuls
got everything back.

171
00:17:35,027 --> 00:17:36,128
Congratulations, boss.

172
00:17:53,019 --> 00:17:56,400
Our daughter never understood

173
00:17:57,136 --> 00:17:58,137
why I did all of this.

174
00:18:04,355 --> 00:18:05,356
Besides,

175
00:18:07,665 --> 00:18:10,560
I don't have to grieve over Blue, do I?

176
00:18:50,744 --> 00:18:51,745
Phu.

177
00:18:55,374 --> 00:18:57,600
Should I send our men
out to look for her, sir?

178
00:19:11,366 --> 00:19:12,600
Don't do a damn thing.

179
00:19:16,262 --> 00:19:18,063
It was all just an act.

180
00:19:19,600 --> 00:19:20,680
Blue is still alive.

181
00:19:31,080 --> 00:19:32,481
[Two Weeks Earlier]

182
00:19:57,174 --> 00:19:58,494
What are we going to do about us?

183
00:20:38,990 --> 00:20:41,400
No matter how much
people tell us what to do,

184
00:20:45,832 --> 00:20:47,880
we're the ones who make
our own choices, right?

185
00:21:01,350 --> 00:21:03,300
But we can't escape the truth, can we?

186
00:21:12,670 --> 00:21:14,200
I'm a Kongpurim,

187
00:21:19,131 --> 00:21:21,132
and you're a Monchaitrakul.

188
00:21:49,926 --> 00:21:51,360
But what if I choose you?

189
00:21:55,227 --> 00:21:56,320
Would you choose me too?

190
00:22:19,065 --> 00:22:23,921
"My little sister shouldn't
have to inherit this hatred."

191
00:22:25,456 --> 00:22:29,200
Tokyo deserves to live the life she wants.

192
00:22:38,155 --> 00:22:39,156
Then...

193
00:22:40,322 --> 00:22:41,602
Promise you won't ever leave me.

194
00:22:42,300 --> 00:22:43,301
I promise.

195
00:23:15,358 --> 00:23:16,359
My dad once told me

196
00:23:19,046 --> 00:23:20,360
that I'm a lot like my mom.

197
00:23:24,326 --> 00:23:25,700
Sometimes I wonder

198
00:23:27,080 --> 00:23:28,560
if he meant my eyes

199
00:23:30,760 --> 00:23:32,000
or maybe my lips.

200
00:23:40,900 --> 00:23:42,401
But I think what makes us most alike

201
00:23:50,019 --> 00:23:52,312
is that we both fell in
love with a Monchaitrakul.

202
00:24:08,779 --> 00:24:12,000
Our story might end in the same
bitter feud between our families

203
00:24:13,600 --> 00:24:15,040
just like it has before.

204
00:24:22,552 --> 00:24:24,300
Are you willing to take that risk with me?

205
00:24:32,763 --> 00:24:34,323
I guess we'll have to take that chance.

206
00:24:37,723 --> 00:24:39,960
Because no matter how
hard you try to push me away,

207
00:24:42,448 --> 00:24:44,249
I'll never let go of your hand.

208
00:24:55,686 --> 00:24:56,687
Okay.

209
00:25:05,622 --> 00:25:07,640
Where the hell did you
get something like this?

210
00:25:07,915 --> 00:25:10,128
I got it from a film set.

211
00:25:10,216 --> 00:25:12,000
I took a gig as an extra.

212
00:25:12,598 --> 00:25:14,240
I've already texted Big.

213
00:25:15,558 --> 00:25:17,278
I told him Pakkard was in another province.

214
00:25:18,267 --> 00:25:19,720
That should buy us some time.

215
00:25:21,100 --> 00:25:22,101
Yeah.

216
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:26,001
Tokyo.

217
00:25:27,280 --> 00:25:29,281
I'm sorry.

218
00:25:33,918 --> 00:25:34,919
Yeah.

219
00:25:36,792 --> 00:25:39,200
So we're good now, right?

220
00:25:40,900 --> 00:25:41,901
No.

221
00:25:43,622 --> 00:25:44,640
I'm still mad at you.

222
00:25:49,392 --> 00:25:51,112
But you're still my friend, no matter what.

223
00:25:56,800 --> 00:25:59,801
And thank you guys so much

224
00:26:01,528 --> 00:26:03,329
for risking your lives to help us.

225
00:26:05,529 --> 00:26:06,530
Sure.

226
00:26:08,392 --> 00:26:09,393
Yeah.

227
00:26:10,067 --> 00:26:11,307
Well, since we're already here,

228
00:26:13,300 --> 00:26:14,670
why don't you two

229
00:26:15,911 --> 00:26:17,520
be our witnesses?

230
00:27:33,355 --> 00:27:34,700
May God bless

231
00:27:36,768 --> 00:27:38,160
the pure love

232
00:27:39,400 --> 00:27:40,700
you two share.

233
00:28:16,300 --> 00:28:17,301
Sweetheart!

234
00:28:21,400 --> 00:28:22,600
What are you doing?

235
00:28:23,792 --> 00:28:26,600
- Mom, please listen to me!
- This isn't safe at all!

236
00:28:27,640 --> 00:28:29,040
If you two stay together like this,

237
00:28:29,174 --> 00:28:31,075
- things will only get worse!
- Mom!

238
00:28:32,659 --> 00:28:33,920
I've made up my mind.

239
00:28:35,640 --> 00:28:37,080
I'm running away with Tokyo.

240
00:29:01,214 --> 00:29:02,215
If you're going to leave,

241
00:29:02,878 --> 00:29:03,998
then leave right now.

242
00:29:05,966 --> 00:29:08,706
You can go to Bangkok or anywhere else.

243
00:29:10,078 --> 00:29:11,398
Just get as far away as possible.

244
00:29:27,078 --> 00:29:28,360
Even if we do that,

245
00:29:29,382 --> 00:29:31,883
someone will find us eventually.

246
00:29:35,078 --> 00:29:36,179
I have a plan.

247
00:29:38,747 --> 00:29:40,048
If you help me,

248
00:29:43,206 --> 00:29:45,480
we can disappear without
anyone ever finding us.

249
00:29:47,368 --> 00:29:48,369
What plan?

250
00:30:08,195 --> 00:30:11,080
I don't want to be hotheaded
and unreasonable like Dad or Yi.

251
00:30:12,606 --> 00:30:14,300
But what you're doing is wrong.

252
00:30:20,107 --> 00:30:21,500
What does being right even mean?

253
00:30:25,248 --> 00:30:28,549
Am I supposed to live a life I didn't
choose, pretending to be someone I'm not?

254
00:30:39,120 --> 00:30:41,240
I don't want to take over
the Kongpurim family.

255
00:30:44,083 --> 00:30:45,280
Not now,

256
00:30:46,659 --> 00:30:48,080
not ever.

257
00:30:49,747 --> 00:30:51,187
What the hell are you talking about?

258
00:31:19,489 --> 00:31:21,200
Haven't you always resented

259
00:31:25,619 --> 00:31:27,720
how Dad never recognized your abilities?

260
00:31:34,726 --> 00:31:36,170
If I were out of the picture,

261
00:31:38,352 --> 00:31:40,040
everything you've ever dreamed of,

262
00:31:41,232 --> 00:31:43,480
including taking over Dad's position,

263
00:31:47,195 --> 00:31:48,400
it would all be yours.

264
00:31:54,278 --> 00:31:56,518
Everything would turn out
just as you've always dreamed.

265
00:32:31,478 --> 00:32:34,680
Pakkard, I thought you'd
never answer my calls again.

266
00:32:35,336 --> 00:32:37,337
The Kongpurims know where you are.

267
00:32:37,651 --> 00:32:38,920
But we've got a plan.

268
00:32:39,620 --> 00:32:40,680
Are you okay with it?

269
00:32:54,016 --> 00:32:56,280
After everything I've done to raise you,

270
00:32:56,918 --> 00:32:58,500
this is how you repay me?

271
00:32:58,560 --> 00:33:00,040
Don't act all nice, you old bastard!

272
00:33:01,355 --> 00:33:03,600
What about your bastard
son Yi killing my father?

273
00:33:03,656 --> 00:33:05,250
Your father deserved to die!

274
00:33:05,520 --> 00:33:07,020
And so do you, bitch!

275
00:33:07,536 --> 00:33:08,856
If you're going to shoot Pakkard,

276
00:33:10,096 --> 00:33:11,397
you'll have to kill me first!

277
00:33:12,984 --> 00:33:15,264
Our plan is to pretend to
fight in front of our families.

278
00:33:16,000 --> 00:33:18,960
How far do we have to take it
to make them believe us?

279
00:33:20,920 --> 00:33:23,115
We'll have to make it look
like we're shooting to kill.

280
00:33:23,139 --> 00:33:25,560
After all, our families have
hated each other for years.

281
00:33:26,286 --> 00:33:28,610
But you're sure about this, right?

282
00:33:29,050 --> 00:33:30,600
If you mess up this time,

283
00:33:31,107 --> 00:33:32,760
Blue could really die, you know!

284
00:33:34,459 --> 00:33:35,800
Of course I'm sure.

285
00:33:46,019 --> 00:33:47,620
Blue! Blue! Blue!

286
00:33:47,955 --> 00:33:48,956
Blue!

287
00:33:49,355 --> 00:33:50,640
Will my death

288
00:33:51,179 --> 00:33:53,040
finally put an end to all this?

289
00:33:53,584 --> 00:33:55,480
Let it end here, Dad.

290
00:33:58,319 --> 00:34:00,640
Blue! Blue! Blue!

291
00:34:01,800 --> 00:34:02,801
Po! You son of a bitch!

292
00:34:03,272 --> 00:34:04,273
Get down!

293
00:34:06,600 --> 00:34:07,930
Tokyo, run!

294
00:34:09,342 --> 00:34:10,560
- Go! - Go!

295
00:34:14,414 --> 00:34:15,415
Stop!

296
00:34:16,451 --> 00:34:17,452
Drop your weapons!

297
00:34:19,419 --> 00:34:20,420
Are you okay?

298
00:34:51,192 --> 00:34:53,112
I'll drive the car to the
police station myself.

299
00:34:53,150 --> 00:34:55,680
You can ride with me or follow me.

300
00:36:09,923 --> 00:36:12,560
Hey! Hurry! Over here!

301
00:36:13,843 --> 00:36:15,600
You can start the boat now.

302
00:36:17,016 --> 00:36:18,017
Hurry up!

303
00:36:18,467 --> 00:36:20,250
Get in! Easy now.

304
00:36:32,500 --> 00:36:33,601
Tokyo and Blue.

305
00:36:34,387 --> 00:36:36,560
We've put our lives
on the line for you two.

306
00:36:37,080 --> 00:36:38,301
Don't let us down, okay?

307
00:36:38,960 --> 00:36:40,120
Make sure you get away.

308
00:36:42,603 --> 00:36:44,600
Thank you guys so much.

309
00:36:45,392 --> 00:36:47,072
Why are you crying?

310
00:36:47,193 --> 00:36:48,840
We'll see each other again someday.

311
00:36:49,382 --> 00:36:51,960
Hurry up and go! Enough
with the sentimental stuff! Go!

312
00:36:52,451 --> 00:36:53,452
You can go now.

313
00:36:53,500 --> 00:36:54,501
Okay, okay.

314
00:37:01,600 --> 00:37:03,040
Take good care of my friend, okay?

315
00:37:10,652 --> 00:37:12,520
Don't forget to come back and visit us!

316
00:37:13,420 --> 00:37:14,640
Bye-bye!

317
00:37:47,496 --> 00:37:50,560
We always remember what we're missing,

318
00:37:51,027 --> 00:37:53,760
but slowly forget what we still have.

319
00:37:54,686 --> 00:37:57,500
Until one day, we're about to lose it.

320
00:38:06,350 --> 00:38:08,190
I've requested a transfer
to another province.

321
00:38:16,123 --> 00:38:17,443
Who gave you permission to leave?

322
00:38:20,107 --> 00:38:22,000
There's an opening in another province.

323
00:38:23,526 --> 00:38:24,840
I want to work on cases there.

324
00:38:27,014 --> 00:38:28,414
I want to make something of myself.

325
00:38:31,894 --> 00:38:33,080
How can you just leave?

326
00:38:34,496 --> 00:38:37,136
- Everything I've built...
- Dad, was I ever even an option to you?

327
00:39:13,832 --> 00:39:15,170
I don't blame you, Dad.

328
00:39:17,440 --> 00:39:18,441
From now on,

329
00:39:21,528 --> 00:39:23,600
I'm going to try to
make my own way in life.

330
00:39:32,859 --> 00:39:34,560
Sometimes we have to lose something

331
00:39:35,360 --> 00:39:36,960
before we realize how much it matters.

332
00:39:44,155 --> 00:39:45,960
In the end, you used our daughter's death

333
00:39:47,366 --> 00:39:48,880
to pin the blame on Tokyo.

334
00:39:49,606 --> 00:39:52,440
Then you used it as leverage
to get everything you wanted.

335
00:39:53,195 --> 00:39:54,196
Isn't that right?

336
00:39:56,864 --> 00:39:58,320
Your success

337
00:40:00,283 --> 00:40:02,280
must mean so much to you.

338
00:40:06,016 --> 00:40:07,696
You don't need me or our daughter anymore.

339
00:40:15,235 --> 00:40:16,500
But how do we know

340
00:40:16,904 --> 00:40:18,650
what's worth holding on to?

341
00:40:38,896 --> 00:40:40,520
No matter what tomorrow brings,

342
00:40:43,035 --> 00:40:45,520
I'm happy today

343
00:40:47,243 --> 00:40:48,480
because I'm here with you.

344
00:40:50,784 --> 00:40:52,424
Why are you only thinking about tomorrow?

345
00:40:53,480 --> 00:40:55,120
Think further ahead.

346
00:40:55,566 --> 00:40:57,880
Once I'm famous and become
a world-renowned artist,

347
00:40:57,950 --> 00:40:59,800
I'll take you around the world!

348
00:40:59,851 --> 00:41:01,320
I'll take you to see seaside towns,

349
00:41:01,408 --> 00:41:03,360
climb volcanoes,

350
00:41:03,409 --> 00:41:05,489
and see the mummies you've
always dreamed of seeing!

351
00:41:13,995 --> 00:41:15,880
But I have a new dream now.

352
00:41:26,768 --> 00:41:28,880
I want to bring you back to this town

353
00:41:30,520 --> 00:41:33,400
to see my mom and Yi.

354
00:41:38,542 --> 00:41:39,880
I want to show them

355
00:41:40,976 --> 00:41:42,440
that our love

356
00:41:43,616 --> 00:41:45,800
is stronger than their hatred.

357
00:41:51,195 --> 00:41:52,715
Let's come back here together someday.

358
00:42:02,043 --> 00:42:03,644
Let's just hope we don't break up.

359
00:42:05,382 --> 00:42:07,520
Otherwise, all this
would've been for nothing.

360
00:42:16,955 --> 00:42:17,956
We won't break up!

361
00:42:19,400 --> 00:42:21,200
No matter what happens,
we'll never break up!

362
00:42:27,032 --> 00:42:28,033
Never.

363
00:42:34,500 --> 00:42:36,080
Are you sure you want to come with me?

364
00:42:38,142 --> 00:42:39,143
Absolutely.

365
00:42:51,304 --> 00:42:55,240
There are three things in life
we should never let ourselves lose.

366
00:42:56,816 --> 00:42:57,920
And they are

367
00:42:59,107 --> 00:43:00,108
faith,

368
00:43:00,920 --> 00:43:01,921
hope,

369
00:43:02,840 --> 00:43:03,880
- and love.
- And love.

370
00:44:04,115 --> 00:44:05,160
Cut!

371
00:44:11,566 --> 00:44:12,567
Cut!

372
00:44:13,518 --> 00:44:14,519
Cut!

373
00:44:21,424 --> 00:44:22,425
Cut!

374
00:44:24,000 --> 00:44:25,440
That was close. Almost there.

375
00:44:31,827 --> 00:44:33,080
One more take. One more.

376
00:44:33,379 --> 00:44:34,379
Who should I look at?

377
00:44:37,278 --> 00:44:39,880
You're hungry, aren't you?
You're just not saying it.

378
00:44:43,992 --> 00:44:44,993
Your hands are so sweaty.

379
00:44:46,083 --> 00:44:47,084
They're all sweaty!

380
00:44:52,814 --> 00:44:55,200
I hope we never break up in the future.

381
00:44:56,000 --> 00:44:57,001
We won't.

382
00:45:00,360 --> 00:45:03,300
Your face suddenly turned green. Wow,
what a mood killer!

383
00:45:03,361 --> 00:45:04,881
The green drink should sponsor us now.

384
00:45:05,580 --> 00:45:07,000
- Cut!
- Cut!

385
00:45:09,286 --> 00:45:10,800
Hey, they've already called cut!

386
00:45:11,262 --> 00:45:12,263
Hey!
